//
// Normative rule Zicfilp_elp_lpad_expected (src/unpriv/cfi.adoc):
//   When elp is set to LP_EXPECTED, if the next instruction in the instruction stream is not 4-byte
//     aligned, or is not lpad, or if the landing pad label encoded in lpad is not zero and does not
//     match the expected landing pad label in bits 31:12 of the x7 register, then a software-check
//     exception (cause=18) with xtval set to "landing pad fault (code=2)" is raised else the elp is
//     updated to NO_LP_EXPECTED.
//
// Context:
//   Landing pads are enabled in every mode. The exception is raised at the target, not at the jump
//     (https://github.com/riscv/riscv-isa-manual/issues/1584: "Its the instruction at the target").
//     xtval may also be 0, the "No information provided" software-check code (machine.adoc,
//     supervisor.adoc).
//
// Clarifications:
//   https://github.com/riscv/riscv-isa-manual/issues/1584: xepc is the target instruction for all
//     three conditions.
//
// Test plan:
//   In U, S, VU and VS (H), after an indirect jump:
//   1. Each condition alone faults with cause 18, xepc = the target, xtval in {0, 2}, xPELP = 1: a
//     non-lpad; a mismatched label; (C) a misaligned lpad 0, and a misaligned lpad with a matching
//     label.
//   2. Otherwise ELP becomes NO_LP_EXPECTED: an ebreak right after the lpad takes a breakpoint with
//     xPELP=0, and a mismatched lpad right after the lpad does not fault.
//
// Approximate dynamic instruction count: 5480
//

